# GitHub Pages on a free account requires a PUBLIC repo, so anything committed
# here is world-readable. The plaintext idea list therefore stays out of git —
# only the encrypted public/ideas.sealed.json is committed, which is what makes
# the access code meaningful. Keep your own copy of # Any idea list, whatever it is called. A file named ideas2.json once sat
# here untracked and would have been committed by the next `git add -A`.
ideas*.json
!public/ideas.sealed.json locally.
ideas.json

